## 6. The `package-artifacts` trap

Checked before and after every run: `grep -c 'Test.equals' samples/boring/MathNaNTestSupport.hx`
= 5 at start, 5 at end; never 0, no git restore needed. My driver does not share the hazard: it
writes nothing outside the gitignored out dir (no tracked file is ever opened for writing, no
`try/finally` needed because there is no save/restore of tracked state). The residual hazard class
is documented in gap-ci-plan §4: `Bun.spawnSync` has no timeout, so a hung `haxe`/`swiftc` would
hang the test process (bun's 60s test timeout abandons the test, "killed 1 dangling process" was
observed in `ciwire-ro-test.log`).

